CRONTAB:-


     A cronjob is a scheduled task that allows you to run scripts or sschedule times without manul interventions
     eg:- backing up files , running sytem maintaince, or sending email reports

COMMANDS:- 
    CRONTAB -E:-
              to edit crontab

    crontab -l:-
              how to view your current cron job

   crontab -r:-
            to delete cron

WHY USE:-
     cron job automate repetitive task ensuring they run at scheduled time without manul intervention

HOW DOES CRON WORK:-
       corn uses a danemon called cron execute scheduled task
       the configrutaion for these is stored in a file called a crontab

    syntax:-

     1.* - minute (0-59)
     2.* - hour (0-23)
     3.* - day of the month (1-31)
     4.* - month (1-12)
     5.* - day of the week (o-7) 





  
           
